{
 "$comment": "Single source of truth for Style Kit component props. The Python pipeline validates every scene spec against these schemas; the prompt shows them to Claude. Logical canvas is 1280x720, origin top-left. Colors are token names: ink, inkSoft, muted, accent, indigo, sage, ochre (or #hex).",
 "common": {
  "id": "unique string, used by `target`/`from`/`to` references",
  "type": "component name below",
  "at": "seconds from scene start when the entrance begins",
  "until": "optional seconds when it fades out (0.35s); omit to stay to the end",
  "dur": "optional entrance duration override (seconds)",
  "fixed": "optional true = ignore camera moves",
  "motion": "Any element may also take `motion`: [{cue|at, dx, dy | x, y, scale, rotate, opacity, dur}] to move/scale/turn it (each key starts a smooth move lasting dur, default 1.2 s; x/y = new centre), and `loop`: bob|float|pulse|breathe|spin|sway|shake for an idle animation after its entrance (`loopSpeed` scales it). Any element may also take `depth` (-1 far … 0 the subject … 1 near): it sets parallax when the camera moves and which plane depth of field blurs (Landscape defaults to -0.7, Guide to 0.35)."
 },
 "components": {
  "TitleCard": {
   "description": "Full-width opening title, hand-written, with a vermilion brush underline. Use once, at the start of a lesson's first scene. Fade it out (until) before other content appears.",
