  "Epithelium": {
   "description": "Cell-level transport across an epithelium (kidney tubule, gut, glands): lumen on the left, 1–3 epithelial cells (apical brush border, nucleus, mitochondria, tight junctions) in the middle, interstitium and a capillary with flowing red cells on the right. Each item of `transporters` appears at its cue on the apical or basolateral membrane (`pos` 0–1 = height) and moves its `carries` through it: ion names (\"Na+\", \"K+\", \"Cl−\", \"H+\", \"Ca2+\", \"HCO3−\") or particle kinds (glucose, water, urea, AA). Cargo moves toward the blood unless toward=\"lumen\"; an exchanger's and a pump's second cargo moves the opposite way (3 Na+ out, 2 K+ in). `paracellular` sends water or ions between the cells. Default box 1080×430 centred at (640,405). Anchors: lumen, cell, nucleus, apical, basolateral, junction, interstitium, blood, transporter0…",
